.skilled/skills/sk-code/feature-catalog/quality-gate/codebase-agnostic-quality-gate.md:34:`--format json|text|envelope` picks the output form, and JSON is the default. The exit code carries the verdict: 0 `NO_BLOCKER_FOUND`, 1 `BLOCKED` for a blocking P0 finding or a failed required P0 configured check, 2 `NOTHING_CHECKED` when no check applied to any file, 3 `ERROR` for a usage or config error or a check that changed the workspace, and 4 `UNVERIFIED` when nothing blocks but a required check produced no evidence or two checklists disagree on a rule. The run verdict has three readers: the verify workflow, the `Quality Gate` field of the @code return and `sk-code-review`, which reads it as input evidence only.
.skilled/skills/sk-code/changelog/v3.4.0.0.md:26:- **The handoffs name the runner.** The implement and debug workflows say the quality mode runs `quality-gate.cjs` first. The verify workflow reads the envelope's `checker_outputs` field and hands back to quality only on `BLOCKED`, `ERROR` or a field still reading `PENDING_AGENT_JUDGMENT`. It handles `UNVERIFIED` and `NOTHING_CHECKED` itself, and it states that the quality config never supplies verification commands.
.skilled/skills/sk-code/shared/references/universal/code-quality-standards.md:169:   It reads the working-tree change by default, or `--files <path>...`, and prints one verdict. Its built-in checks cover the mechanical floor in §3, and the comment-hygiene checker is one of its sensors, so one run checks both. Zero blocking findings are required. `BLOCKED` stops completion until the finding is fixed, and `UNVERIFIED` or `NOTHING_CHECKED` never reads as clean. To suppress a known comment-hygiene false positive, put `hygiene-ok` on that comment line. The gate values and the verdict fields are in `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-quality/references/runner-contract.md`.
.skilled/skills/sk-code/shared/references/workflow-verify.md:56:2. Read the implementation, quality or debug handoff for the intended behavior, changed scope, baseline and accepted risks. From the quality envelope, read the `checker_outputs` field with the `gate` and `unverified` values it carries, and any field that still reads `PENDING_AGENT_JUDGMENT`. Hand back to quality only on `BLOCKED`, `ERROR` or a field still reading `PENDING_AGENT_JUDGMENT`, which is the 3 to 1.5 transition in [phase-detection.md](../../shared/references/phase-detection.md). On `UNVERIFIED`, prove each id it lists with this phase's own command or report that id open. On `NOTHING_CHECKED`, prove the claim with this phase's own commands and never read the gate as clean, because no check read any file as code, which is where a Markdown-only change lands. The run verdict has three readers: this step, the @code RETURN `Quality Gate` field and `sk-code-review`, which reads it as input evidence only.
